# Detection Engineering

This section contains example detection logic that can be used to identify attacker activity observed during the Tempest Incident Response investigation.

---

# Splunk Queries

## 1. PowerShell Spawned by Microsoft Word

Detects PowerShell executed from Microsoft Word, which is commonly associated with malicious Office documents and macros.

```spl
index=sysmon EventCode=1
Image="*powershell.exe"
ParentImage="*WINWORD.EXE"
```

**MITRE ATT&CK:** T1566.001, T1059.001

---

## 2. PowerShell Download Activity

Detects PowerShell downloading additional payloads from the Internet.

```spl
index=sysmon EventCode=1
Image="*powershell.exe"
(CommandLine="*DownloadString*" OR
 CommandLine="*Invoke-WebRequest*" OR
 CommandLine="*Net.WebClient*" OR
 CommandLine="*iwr*")
```

**MITRE ATT&CK:** T1105

---

## 3. PowerShell Network Connections

Shows outbound network connections initiated by PowerShell.

```spl
index=sysmon EventCode=3
Image="*powershell.exe"
```

**MITRE ATT&CK:** T1071

---

## 4. Service Creation

Detects creation of new Windows services.

```spl
index=wineventlog EventCode=7045
```

or

```spl
index=sysmon EventCode=1
CommandLine="*sc.exe create*"
```

**MITRE ATT&CK:** T1543

---

## 5. Registry Run Key Persistence

Detects persistence through Windows Run registry keys.

```spl
index=sysmon EventCode=13
TargetObject="*\\CurrentVersion\\Run*"
```

**MITRE ATT&CK:** T1547

---

## 6. WMIC Execution

Detects execution of Windows Management Instrumentation Command-line.

```spl
index=sysmon EventCode=1
Image="*wmic.exe"
```

**MITRE ATT&CK:** T1047

---

## 7. Executables Running from Temp Folder

Detects executables launched from temporary directories.

```spl
index=sysmon EventCode=1
Image="*\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\*"
```

**MITRE ATT&CK:** T1204

---

## 8. Certutil Download Activity

Detects Certutil downloading remote files.

```spl
index=sysmon EventCode=1
Image="*certutil.exe"
CommandLine="*urlcache*"
```

**MITRE ATT&CK:** T1105

