## Lessons Learned

The Tempest investigation highlighted several behaviors that can be monitored proactively within a SIEM.

Creating detection rules based on attacker TTPs improves visibility, accelerates incident response, and reduces mean time to detect (MTTD).

These example queries and Sigma rules demonstrate how observed attacker activity can be translated into practical detection logic suitable for SOC operations.
